---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro'
import FAQItem from '../components/FAQItem.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
---
<Base title="FAQ — Owen & Rowan" description="Attire, weather, transportation, food, and other things you might be wondering.">
  <Breadcrumb />

  <article class="px-6 max-w-2xl mx-auto pb-24">

    <h1 class="type-display mb-16" style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);" data-reveal>
      FAQ
    </h1>

    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="type-label mb-6" style="color: var(--c-terracotta);" data-reveal>Before You Arrive</h2>

      <FAQItem question="What should I wear?">
        <p>
          Cocktail attire — dressy but not over the top. Linen suits and sundresses are very
          much welcomed. The ceremony is in a courtyard in New Mexico in July, which means
          it will be warm in the early evening. Santa Fe cools down quickly after sunset,
          especially after a thunderstorm, so bring a light layer for later in the night.
          This is a wedding, not a gala. Wear something you feel good in.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>

      <FAQItem question="What if it rains?">
        <p>
          July is monsoon season in New Mexico. Afternoon thunderstorms are common — they
          come in fast, drop significant rain, and clear quickly. If there's weather at
          ceremony time, we move inside the museum. The building is beautiful either way,
          and New Mexico rain is brief and dramatic. We're not worried, and you shouldn't be either.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>

      <FAQItem question="When should I RSVP by?">
        <p>
          June 11, 2026. Please don't wait until the last minute — we need an accurate
          headcount well before the wedding. If your plans change after you've responded,
          let us know as soon as possible.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="type-label mb-6" style="color: var(--c-terracotta);" data-reveal>Getting Around</h2>

      <FAQItem question="How do I get to the venue?">
        <p>
          The New Mexico Museum of Art is at 107 W Palace Ave, one block from the Plaza in
          downtown Santa Fe. If you're staying at a Plaza-area hotel, it's a short walk.
          Street parking on Palace Ave fills early on summer evenings. The Santa Fe Place
          Mall parking structure on Sandoval St is a short walk away.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>

      <FAQItem question="What about Uber / Lyft?">
        <p>
          Uber and Lyft both operate in Santa Fe, but supply is limited compared to a major
          city — especially for late-night pickups after an event ends. If you're planning
          to drink and don't have a designated driver, budget extra wait time or arrange
          a car service in advance. The Plaza hotels are all walkable from the venue.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="type-label mb-6" style="color: var(--c-terracotta);" data-reveal>The Evening</h2>

      <FAQItem question="What's the timeline for the evening?">
        <p>
          Doors open at 5:45 pm. Ceremony begins at 6:00 pm. Cocktail hour from 7:00 pm,
          followed by dinner and dancing at 8:00 pm. The evening wraps up at 11:00 pm.
          The Plaza is five minutes on foot if the night has more in it.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>

      <FAQItem question="What will there be to eat?">
        <p>
          Catering is being finalized — we'll update this page and the Venue page with
          full menu details when they're confirmed. We're collecting dietary restrictions
          via the RSVP form and they will be accommodated.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>

      <FAQItem question="What about drinks?">
        <p>
          There will be a full bar at cocktail hour and dinner. More details to come as
          catering is confirmed.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>

      <FAQItem question="What music will there be?">
        <p>
          Still finalizing music details. Submit a song request with your RSVP and we'll
          do our best. We'll update this page when confirmed.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="type-label mb-6" style="color: var(--c-terracotta);" data-reveal>The Fine Print</h2>

      <FAQItem question="Can I bring a plus one?">
        <p>
          Please check your invitation — it will specify whether your invitation includes
          a plus one. If you have questions about this, reach out to us directly before
          submitting your RSVP.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>

      <FAQItem question="Are kids welcome?">
        <p>
          The wedding is adults only, with exceptions for close family. If you have
          questions about whether your children are included, please ask us directly
          rather than assuming either way.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>

      <FAQItem question="Is the venue accessible?">
        <p>
          We're confirming specific accessibility details for the NMMA courtyard and
          will update this page with that information. If you have particular accessibility
          needs, please reach out directly and we'll make sure you have what you need.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>

      <FAQItem question="What's your policy on phones during the ceremony?">
        <p>
          We'd love for you to be present. Please keep phones away during the ceremony
          itself — there will be a photographer capturing everything. After the ceremony,
          take all the photos you want and share them however you like.
        </p>
      </FAQItem>
    </section>

  </article>

  <Footer />
</Base>
